<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mixed, movement thin.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mixed, movement thin.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were mixed on Wednesday and movement was thin as farmers focused on field work, several cash dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We've got the sun shining and hopefully the fields will dry out enough that they (farmers) can get out there,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said. &quot;Most of the grain is in the ground but they're still pretty busy planting beans.&quot;</p>
<p>A drop in MGE spring wheat futures virtually halted sales, prompting some locations to increase basis bids to try to attract selling interest. One Montana dealer said his firm raised basis bids by five cents.</p>
<p>&quot;They're still not selling,&quot; he said.  </p>
